  {
    "field_name": "Raw Output Example",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "sample_index,status,collective,num_gpus,bytes,allreduce_busbw_gb_s,allreduce_algbw_gb_s,allreduce_latency_at_min_bytes_us,error_message\n0,ok,all_reduce,1,1024,na (requires at least two GPUs),na (requires at least two GPUs),na (requires at least two GPUs),"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Output Fields / Metrics to Parse",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "collective, num_gpus (GPUs used), bytes (largest size), allreduce_busbw_gb_s and allreduce_algbw_gb_s (at the largest size), allreduce_latency_at_min_bytes_us (at the smallest size)"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Parser and Normalization Notes",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Below two GPUs each metric is the text na (requires at least two GPUs), and summary.json reports that text. bin/nccl_bw uses the nccl-tests busbw factors: 2(n-1)/n for all_reduce, (n-1)/n for all_gather and reduce_scatter, 1 for broadcast and reduce. The collector publishes all_reduce only. Every size is in nccl_sweep.csv"
  },
  {
